  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "CooperVision consumption growth (mid-single-digit per management) reappears in reported revenue after the FY2026 US channel inventory reduction laps; MiSight grows ~15-20% ex-China; CooperSurgical fertility offsets IUD competition. Revenue compounds ~4-5% for five years, fading to 3%; pre-SBC EBITDA margin drifts from 31% to 32.5% as capex steps down from the FY2023-25 capacity build (10.9% -> ~6%). Cash tax follows guidance to ~17.5-18%.",
    "bull": "Myopia management is the axis: MiSight/MyDay MiSight approvals in Japan, UK and Europe and a China recovery turn it into a multi-hundred-million-dollar double-digit grower; the expanded US sales footprint and pulled-forward pipeline regain share in torics/multifocals; fertility genomics compounds. Growth 6.5-7% for four years, margins to 34.5%, capex to 5.5%.",
    "bear": "Contact-lens share loss to J&J Vision and Alcon is structural, not timing; China myopia stays soft and competitors narrow MiSight's clinical lead; Paragard's monopoly ends and the MDL (4,000+ cases, exposure potentially above insurance) produces further settlements beyond the $272M net accrual already deducted. Growth ~2.5%, margin compresses to 29.5%, cash tax 20%, 14x terminal cap."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Unlevered owner-FCF DCF with SBC and equity-award withholding taxes expensed and the share count held flat (Cooper is an active repurchaser). Margins built from GAAP-inclusive components so Cooper's recurring 'one-time' charges stay in the flows; the one quantified litigation liability is deducted in the bridge. Street basis (SBC as non-cash) reported as a memo band.",
